{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>None [shall slumber] etc.</b> ינום, lighten of יישן, and the meaning: he shall not slumber even though he may sleep." "And נתק is not from the nifal binyan."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {0 "Reading קל מישן as 'light/defective of יישן'; the comparison presumes the longer form has yod as mater lectionis.", 1 "The referent of נתק is uncertain; it may concern a form in the preceding clause or a textual variant in the verse."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:23.825043078Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}